{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/camera.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:28:47.874454Z","id":"08ce04b2383752b3669f6be07dbe62378bed7769ba181ee277fb03fddd37525c","body":{"detail":"Focus is the 10th-90th percentile box of changed pixels (camera.change_boxes), pooled over 0.6 s. Seen on the cut of 2026-10-27 (coldopen, agent, dash, globe, game, realtime, history, claxbot, share): in realtime the box swings between the checklist cursors and Mia's draft in the thread panel, so the 4 s insert pans across the page (capped at INSERT_ZOOM_MAX 1.35 to keep it readable); in the lead-in of every ask the pointer's travel to the Comment button draws a 1.1-1.3x zoom before the drawing starts; after the globe and game reveals the continuous animation (spinning globe, moving stars) is itself the largest change, so the touch framing centres on it rather than on the hover. A per-vignette focus hint (a region or a beat-to-region map in beats.json) would steer these.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"e3d95dbb7a1622d4b51506e61643c0bef1b415e6d1018b85d6fe862668e9f96f"},"summary":"The camera follows whatever changes most, which is not always the story beat","tags":["reel","camera","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/camera.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:28:47.874515Z","id":"98e974ebefd2825ebcbba00ea7466c3b022b1779b9a09f23f52eaca5341f5598","body":{"detail":"With the focus on the thread panel (claxbot's ClaxBot panel, share's thread), the spotlit box covers the right third and the dimmed rest includes the page itself; it reads as a grey band at the left edge rather than as emphasis. SPOT_MAX_AREA fades it as the box grows, but a tall narrow panel box stays under the threshold. Options: spotlight only boxes in the page area, or drop it below some aspect ratio.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"946edd6bb2d11ece665b736353834ba5c8aca26262cbfc2c17dabc139a209a00"},"summary":"The spotlight darkens real content when the focus is a side panel","tags":["reel","camera","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/compose.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:28:47.874547Z","id":"1703bccee78a9d49c1195d02f4598798348c9ea79acc5b169d0d30c8ca84ca5d","body":{"detail":"compose.sh builds clax-reel.gif from each vignette's reveal window straight from FRAMES_DIR/frames, so it shows neither the crop path (OUT/camera/*.tsv) nor the teaser/intro the mp4 opens with. Around the reveal the camera is at 1.0 anyway, so the frames mostly match; cutting the GIF from the rendered clips by cut.json's reveal t_clip would make the two agree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":289},"end":{"line":300},"content_hash":"1bdd7a7401c23ef24de3d8de60fd6ca63cb39b0802c61273480d083abd5ba2bb"},"summary":"The GIF is cut from the raw frames, without the camera, teaser or intro","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/compose.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T20:28:47.874570Z","id":"ebf79fcc2f64f28150d6eb2f211c38a7071dbb63bbb00c4d6c66dcbf666de3fa","body":{"detail":"camera.py renders each output frame with Pillow (bicubic affine, sub-pixel) and pipes rgb24 to ffmpeg, which needs numpy and Pillow: compose.sh makes target/reel-venv with pinned numpy 2.0.2 and Pillow 11.3.0 from PyPI on first use. ffmpeg's crop takes integer offsets per frame and changing its size per frame re-initialises scale, so slow drifts judder by a source pixel; Pillow avoids both. The diff analysis also uses numpy.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"15da401d50264691d413eb314393b5d66fcee3de13dd0db52e86c4a0c73962f6"},"summary":"Render the camera with ffmpeg crop/scale driven by sendcmd instead of Pillow","tags":["reel","revisit:the composer must run without network access or a Python venv","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/camera.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T21:43:53.678052Z","id":"2c4e87f57774f1776075ef780d81fbe6312cf53ce1fb49b22cfad77719ae2dfd","body":{"detail":"Only the opt-in --camera-motion path has this spotlight now (the default is the focus treatment in camera.focus_path). With the focus on a thread panel (claxbot's ClaxBot panel, share's thread), the spotlit box covers the right third and the dimmed rest includes the page; it reads as a grey band at the left edge. SPOT_MAX_AREA fades it as the box grows, but a tall narrow panel box stays under the threshold.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"946edd6bb2d11ece665b736353834ba5c8aca26262cbfc2c17dabc139a209a00"},"summary":"Under --camera-motion, the spotlight darkens real content when the focus is a side panel","supersedes":"98e974ebefd2825ebcbba00ea7466c3b022b1779b9a09f23f52eaca5341f5598","tags":["reel","camera","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/camera.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T21:43:53.760830Z","id":"b1cfcf9b382893128f06defc0431f31b31a03b1af6eb698e22cefc9e2eb46f11","body":{"detail":"Seen rendering coldopen, agent, dash, globe, game, realtime, history, claxbot and share (see OUT/camera/*.tsv): in dash the first region, at the start of the drawing, is a strip of the table's header rows (x 0-1122, y 95-265) for about 1.4 s before the drawn area replaces it; where the composer floats over a dense table (dash, globe) snap cannot separate its card from the table and the region is the textarea only; in share the comment beat's region is the anchored KPI card, not Priya's typing in the panel; realtime's 4 s insert changes region three times. A per-vignette focus hint in beats.json (a region per beat) would settle these.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":577},"end":{"line":687},"content_hash":"1801f74cc857fadd716e4dac2ae327d3979cfb3fb0cc51f627e7ca78f5dce600"},"summary":"The focus region is inferred from pixel change, and some vignettes get a weaker region than the beat deserves","supersedes":"08ce04b2383752b3669f6be07dbe62378bed7769ba181ee277fb03fddd37525c","tags":["reel","camera","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/compose/compose.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T21:43:53.842703Z","id":"65bd274ddf237c41dd89399c0112a14f6783325a05595182d98dc9996a2dbc0a","body":{"detail":"compose.sh now builds clax-reel.gif from the x264 clips so it carries the treatment; the decoded frames' compression noise defeats paletteuse's diff_mode=rectangle, so most of every frame is re-encoded. Rendering the GIF's frames straight from camera.py render (no x264 in between) would bring the size back down.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":340},"content_hash":"e254a7625930e0180bd1946e12479a69d79ea475219f7b03180b5478185651e9"},"summary":"The GIF grew from about 2.2 MB to 5.7 MB once cut from the rendered clips","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
